        "original_id": "a60a25cd-bc5d-56a6-a2d2-a5cc73403bba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Sayidaty, Closer, Hia, Al Jamila\n- People: Mai Badr, Lida Fleitmann Bloodgood\n- Companies: Bauer Media Group\n- Places: Dubai, Beirut, the Middle East, North Africa, Europe, America\n- Roles: editor-in-chief, deputy editor-in-chief, author, horsewoman\n\nFacts:\n- Lida Louise Fleitmann Bloodgood lived from 1894 to 1982 and was an author and a horsewoman in America and Europe.\n- Mai Badr was born on 6 July 1968.\n- Sayidaty is a women’s magazine whose Arabic title means “My Lady” in English.\n- Sayidaty is published weekly in Arabic and monthly in English.\n- Sayidaty is published in Dubai and Beirut and is distributed throughout the Middle East, North Africa, Europe, and America.\n- Closer is a British tabloid magazine published by Bauer Media Group.\n- Mai Badr is the editor-in-chief of Hia magazine and the deputy editor-in-chief of Sayidaty and Al Jamila.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
